# Test-driven development

Write or update tests **before** (or as the driver for) production code changes.

## What to test

- Observable **behaviour** and contracts: inputs → outputs, user-visible results, invariants, error cases.
- Discoverability: a UI or API built by introspection should still work when new processes/states appear, without rewriting the test around private helpers.

## What not to test

- Private helpers, call order, exact class structure, or incidental formatting unless that formatting is part of the product contract.
- Framework wiring (NiceGUI widget trees, mock internals) when a higher-level behavioural check covers the same outcome.

## Style

- Name tests after the behaviour (`test_simulation_history_exposes_clock_step_series`), not after methods (`test_inspect_process`).
- Prefer the smallest real fixture that exhibits the behaviour (e.g. clock-only model) over mocks of collaborators.
- One behaviour per test; assert outcomes, not how they were computed.
